    "narrative": "Today's optimal lineup is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts the day\u2019s highest efficiency at 81.07. His matchup against Singer is elevated by a strong BvP history and a favorable #2 spot in the order, making him our premier offensive engine. **Cal Raleigh** (76.47) and **Daulton Varsho** (72.31) also provide elite stability; **Cal Raleigh** leverages a significant platoon advantage against Lauer, while **Daulton Varsho** benefits from a soft matchup against Littell and a strong dynamic platoon adjustment. **Gleyber Torres** also warrants attention as a top-tier play (67.52) today, as his projection sees a substantial +13% bump due to the favorable platoon split against Rogers.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Gavin Sheets**, who fell just short of the 45.14 mark required to displace our lower-tier starters. While he held a decent projection against Hughes, he ultimately couldn't overcome the efficiency floor set by the rest of our active roster. Conversely, we are carrying some risk in the outfield: **Taylor Ward** is forced into a challenging matchup against the elite arm of Skubal, resulting in a muted score of 53.36, though we keep him active for his lead-off volume. Similarly, **Luis Arraez** (58.48) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (51.86) face the soft matchup of Pannone, but both suffer from negative platoon impacts that dampen their ceiling. Monitor **Geraldo Perdomo** (45.33), as his matchup against the strong arm of Jones places him on the extreme edge of our starting threshold; he remains active, but serves as our primary candidate for mid-game defensive replacement if the game script turns stagnant.",
